avs3a: Audio Vivid decoded, from FFmpeg pull request 25207

Audio Vivid (菁彩声, AVS3-P3) is the sound China's 4K and 8K channels
carry beside an AAC track, and on some channels in its place. FFmpeg
9.0.2 has no decoder for it. This is Peter Ross's decoder, parser and
readers as pull request 25207 had them on 2026-11-20, at its head
2456ca9bc5dba71997c0bd2c4186c93c6a6dd405:
https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/25207. On 2026-11-23 it was
open and not merged, and every approval of it was a review bot's. It is
LGPL 2.1 or later, written from the published standard T/AI 109.3-2023,
whose Annex B its tables come from.

What it decodes: mono, stereo, 5.1, 7.1, 5.1.2, 5.1.4, 7.1.2 and 7.1.4,
objects (as further channels, with nothing said of where they are), and
HOA of orders 1 to 3 (as ambisonic channels). 10.2, 22.2 and 4.0 are
asked for as samples and not decoded.

What was changed to carry it to 9.0.2, and nothing else: its entries in
Changelog and doc/APIchanges and its two version bumps are left out, and
so are its FATE tests, whose samples this build does not fetch; and the
layouts 5.1.4 and 7.1.4 are named as 9.0.2 names them,
AV_CHANNEL_LAYOUT_5POINT1POINT4_BACK and 7POINT1POINT4_BACK. Those hold
the same channels as master's AV_CHANNEL_LAYOUT_5POINT1POINT4 and
7POINT1POINT4, of which master keeps the old names as aliases.

When FFmpeg has it in a release, this patch goes and the release comes.

